      "message": "Usually I prefer to put everything at top level, and make \"inner\" classes as typedefs. e.g.\n\n```\nclass AbcInnerClass { ... };\n\nclass Abc {\npublic: \n  using InnerClass \u003d AbcInnerClass;\n};\n```\n\nThis lets you forward declare the inner class when you need to.\nHowever, I\u0027m not sure if it\u0027d be possible in this scenario, since we have an inner-inner class that needs to hold an `Abc`. I\u0027d need to experiment with it.",
